description:
Archaeological projects have been undertaken at Highwic in recent years which have brought to light hundreds, if not thousands, of artefacts. These help us piece together information about how the family lived, the history of the site, and where particular structures were located.&nbsp;
Join archaeologist Caroline Phillips for an afternoon at Highwic to view some of these artefacts, learn more about what has been found, and what has not been found. This will be an informal talk, a walk around the site, and an opportunity to view the artefacts.&nbsp;
For more information contact highwic@heritage.org.nz.

Have you ever wondered what it's like to be an archaeologist? What is archaeology? What do archaeologists do?
Join us during Archaeology Week for a chance to be an archaeologist for the day and explore the fascinating world of uncovering history.&nbsp;
Learn about the methods and technology used by archaeologists. Solve puzzles and discover how people used to live, what they ate and what tools they used.
Join us in the Orientation Space in the South Atrium to meet our archaeologists and try hands-on activities such as bone and shell sorting, reconstructing pottery and much more!&nbsp;

May the 4th be with you! OK, OK, it's actually on the 3rd, but that's no biggie.
Use cardboard to make your weapons, space craft, or armor... and then we'll have a battle!
You are encouraged to come in Star Wars costume. &nbsp;
Suitable for ages 8-14.
Drop-off session (although grown-ups can stay if they are super fans).&nbsp;&nbsp;
It is expected that all creations will be dismantled/destroyed in combat. (Creations won't be taken home),
Battle will take place from 3pm-3.30pm, hopefully outdoors depending on the weather. Parents are welcome to return at 3pm to witness the battle. &nbsp;&nbsp;
Free thanks to Devonport-Takapuna Local Board and Resource Recovery Devonport.
Limited numbers, get in quick!
